<h4>D. Lectio Divina &mdash; Your First Attempt</h4>
<p>Try the ancient practice of <em>lectio divina</em> (sacred reading) this week. Pick a short passage (try Mark 1:9-11, the Baptism of Jesus). Follow these four steps:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Lectio (Read):</strong> Read the passage slowly, twice. What word or phrase catches your attention?</li>
<li><strong>Meditatio (Meditate):</strong> Why does that word or phrase stand out? What might God be saying to you through it?</li>
<li><strong>Oratio (Pray):</strong> Speak to God about what you've read. Tell him what's in your heart.</li>
<li><strong>Contemplatio (Contemplate):</strong> Be still. Rest in God's presence. Don't try to figure anything out. Just be with him.</li>
</ol>
<p>Write a short summary of your lectio divina experience here:</p>
